  "screenwriter_raw": "{\n  \"pseudos\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p1\",\n      \"text\": \"The casting decision at the center of the dispute saw Lupita Nyong'o assigned dual roles in Christopher Nolan's upcoming Homer adaptation. This cultural event drew intense online engagement, as prominent commentators accused the film production of erasing European history. Their public allegations of historical erasure became a central accusation, while defenders presented a counter-argument about shared heritage. The resulting public debate now frames the mythic epic as a flashpoint over identity and who may claim classical stories in mass-market film.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.78,\n      \"center\": \"how-2\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-0\", \"how-1\", \"how-2\", \"why-0\", \"result-0\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p2\",\n      \"text\": \"Amid fierce online attacks drawn by the casting news, a central accusation emerged: claims of historical erasure. These allegations requiring evidence were leveled against the production by media professionals in the digital public sphere. Concurrently, defenders argued a perspective grounded in inclusive interpretation, treating the Western canon as shared civilizational heritage. This clash of arguments has ignited a broader cultural conflict, transforming a film project into a societal debate over cultural narratives.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.72,\n      \"center\": \"why-0\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"how-1\", \"why-0\", \"why-1\", \"result-1\"]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p3\",\n      \"text\": \"A rebuttal based on a view of shared heritage was offered by those arguing for diverse casting. They countered the central accusation of historical erasure with an evidence-based counter-narrative, defending the inclusive interpretation of the Western canon. This defense statement, presented in the online dispute venue, directly engages with the public accusations made by commentators. The resulting ideological conflict highlights competing claims to cultural heritage within a contemporary film adaptation.\",\n      \"fit\": 0.75,\n      \"center\": \"how-3\",\n      \"channel\": \"toned\",\n      \"source\": {\n        \"fragments\": [\"why-0\", \"why-1\", \"how-3\", \"result-1\"]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}",
